{"rows":[{"id":"clinical/sunscreen","slot":"actives","finding":"Daily broad-spectrum sunscreen is the strongest-supported routine anchor for preventing photoaging; the retrieved randomized community trial assigned 903 adults younger than 55 to daily broad-spectrum sunscreen versus discretionary use.","status":"measured_result","support":[{"url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23732711/","title":"Sunscreen and prevention of skin aging: a randomized trial","passage":"Randomized, controlled, community-based intervention ... 903 adults younger than 55 years ... Random assignment into 4 groups: daily use of broad-spectrum sunscreen.","sourceType":"Randomized controlled trial abstract"}],"method":"Community RCT in Nambour, Australia; transfer to a Romanian facial routine is plausible for broad UV photoprotection but does not establish an exact facial application quantity here.","comparability":"Both shortlisted sunscreens are retailer-listed SPF50+ PA++++ products, but no head-to-head performance study was retrieved.","confidence":"Moderate-to-high for daily broad-spectrum sunscreen as the anchor; no claim that the more expensive sunscreen is more effective.","disposition":"retain"},{"id":"clinical/retinoid","slot":"actives","finding":"Topical retinoids are strongly recommended in the AAD acne guideline; cosmetic retinol is therefore used as the single evening treatment, while finished-product and photoaging superiority claims remain qualified.","status":"recommendation","support":[{"url":"https://www.jaad.org/article/S0190-9622(23)03389-3/fulltext","title":"Guidelines of care for the management of acne vulgaris","passage":"Strong recommendations are made for benzoyl peroxide, topical retinoids, topical antibiotics, and oral doxycycline. Conditional recommendations are made for ... salicylic acid ...","sourceType":"Dermatology clinical guideline"},{"url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8750127/","title":"A Clinician's Guide to Topical Retinoids","passage":"Reti